  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "IMLOG10 multiplies Excel LN(|re|) by LOG10_E on the real axis and divides IMLN(z) by CRT ln(10) off-axis",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20430 and 20527, IMLOG10(inumber) rejects 0 with #NUM!. When im = 0, its real component is RN53(RN64(excel_log(|re|) * LOG10_E)) (while the imaginary part for re < 0 is pi / crt_log(10)); off the real axis (im != 0), both components divide IMLN(z) by crt_log(10). All 1,209 full-bank and 1,323 pinned IMLOG10 rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in CalcFunc-Evidence cache/w111-extended-regenerated-20260929/answers-imlog10.json.gz (Excel 16.0 build 20430) and Excel 16.0.20527 (witnesses/IMLOG10.json fn10-log10-discriminators); 1,209/1,209 full-bank and 1,323/1,323 pinned rows match.",
